      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T02:10:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why require pinned clang? Tint has been built this way from the start without requiring a specific clang. We got a handful of errors but we just added suppressions (or fixed them) and folks could still turn of everything manually.",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d8ec647_89a9b419",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T17:58:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe it\u0027s overly cautious but I don\u0027t want the build to break just because we\u0027re using a system clang that has slightly different behavior for an obscure warning. I think the `-Wall -Wextra` analyses can be considered stable but not everything else.\n\nAlso we don\u0027t want to get \"error: unknown warning option\" if we pass a `-Wno-*` that an older compiler doesn\u0027t understand.\n\nI guess if Tint has been doing it then it\u0027s fine, but seems like we may as well just do the theoretically safer thing.",
      "parentUuid": "7e3ae4ee_48e62101",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3664b346_c68e4b9e",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T18:04:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We turned off the unknown warning option because it didn\u0027t seem useful.\n\nIt came up a couple of times, but folks could always turn everything off as it was a flag, or we just add the suppression. Seemed more useful to always turn it on in general.",
      "parentUuid": "5d8ec647_89a9b419",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "682978b4_36bf0ff4",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T21:49:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair points and since this is GN, it\u0027s probably very rare to build with anything other than pinned clang.\n\nHow about `dawn_weverything` defaults to `is_clang`, and then before enabling `-Weverything` we do this:\n```\nassert(using_pinned_clang, \"dawn_weverything requires using the pinned clang binary. Disable it if you intend to build with another clang installation.\")\n```\nThat way it reduces the risk we accidentally disable `-Weverything` due to computing `using_pinned_clang` wrong, and if anyone does want to build with non-pinned clang (which should be rare) then they\u0027ll know what to do.",
      "parentUuid": "3664b346_c68e4b9e",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2cc9d3f_91442470",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-19T00:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "682978b4_36bf0ff4",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f36e0be1_8d956244",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002761
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-19T00:41:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t that mean you can never build with Weverything with non-pinned clang? I don\u0027t think that\u0027s necessarily what we want. Or, does the `assert` not stop the build? If it\u0027s just a warning that\u0027s cool.",
      "parentUuid": "c2cc9d3f_91442470",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b0c8fe8_8cce8fdd",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-19T01:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a hard error. For a warning we\u0027d need `print()` but a warning doesn\u0027t seem that useful.\n\nI\u0027ve managed to think of a more concrete scenario for the thing I\u0027m worrying about. It seems to me that if we always enable `-Weverything` in GN, then we will prevent any new version of Clang that adds a new warning from rolling into Chromium. It will have to be suppressed in Dawn, Dawn roll into Chromium, then Chromium can roll Clang.\n\nThough I\u0027m realizing now that `using_pinned_clang` probably is not the right check for that. I don\u0027t even know whether that would be true or false in a chromium build.\n\nOriginally I was thinking about people using system clang, but it seems the only way to do that is to [set a custom clang](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/clang.md#using-a-custom-clang-binary) and I don\u0027t think we need to worry about that.\n\nAnyway I\u0027m not sure the best solution. I don\u0027t want to disable `-Weverything` in `dawn_standalone` because that makes it hard to develop on Dawn in-place in Chromium. But maybe the best we can do is default it off, and people can explicitly enable `dawn_weverything` if they are doing that? I don\u0027t think we have any other good signal whether or not a Chromium build is for someone who is working on Dawn.",
      "parentUuid": "f36e0be1_8d956244",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "152f376a_4f253005",
